id: E999
draft: true
trigger_tool: conan|test|zip|cvs|rcs
phase: testing
error_signature: "missing file .*/stream|MISSING FILE .*/c.md5|MISSING FILE .*/dump|upstream regression corpus unavailable"
severity: 2
category: upstream-test, fixture-provenance, archive-recovery
match_keywords: CVS, RCS, head deltatext, upstream regression, external fixtures, mpeg2dec-streams, IGNORE-MD5, strict denominator, c.md5, dump
title: Recover a complete external regression corpus from the upstream CVS snapshot, not a partial mirror
root_cause: >
  The upstream source archive lists 73 stream cases in test/tests but does not
  ship their stream/c.md5/dump files. The historical external tarball is no
  longer reachable, while a later media mirror contains only a subset and
  different reference c.md5 values. Upstream test/regression prints missing
  fixture messages without necessarily returning failure, so its exit status
  alone can falsely certify an incomplete suite.
affected_scope: >
  Legacy projects whose official test data lived in an external CVS/SVN module
  and whose later mirrors preserve incomplete or mixed-version references.
verification_cmd: >
  Compare all upstream test IDs against the CVS archive's RCS members, verify
  the snapshot SHA-256 and ZIP CRC, restore each head deltatext, then demand
  exact stream/c.md5/dump inventory before executing every case.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: sha-pinned-cvs-rcs-fulltext-and-strict-inventory
rec_description: >
  Obtain a project-owned CVS snapshot, pin its SHA-256, enumerate the upstream
  test manifest, and read the head revision's first RCS deltatext as fulltext
  for every required fixture. Preserve same-snapshot references and upstream
  IGNORE-MD5 markers. Fail if any expected file is missing, changed, or a test
  exits nonzero; count case PASS only after the upstream reference checks.
  A complete small official sample may additionally be embedded byte-for-byte
  with provenance and SHA-256 for an installed-package decode/output/readback
  consumer. Preserve the full upstream denominator, pin the reference CPU
  path for cross-architecture pixel comparison, and distinguish display width
  from the aligned converted-frame stride.
rec_command: >
  python3 testdata/extract-cvs-73.py --zip libmpeg2.zip --tests test/tests
  --output cvs-suite && python3 testdata/run-upstream-73.py
  --decoder src/mpeg2dec --data-root cvs-suite
  --manifest cvs-suite/manifest.tsv --upstream-tests test/tests
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual-corpus-provenance-and-conan-build-test
forbid_1_pattern: "partial mirror.*full upstream PASS|test/regression exit 0.*73/73"
forbid_1_reason: >
  A subset or the upstream shell exit code without input closure does not
  prove that all declared cases were executed with their matching references.
similar_to: [E072, E268, E311]
conflicts_with: []
notes: >
  Dedup: E072/E268 cover Autotools triplet validation; E311 covers Conan
  source-copy isolation. None covers RCS fixture recovery, same-snapshot
  reference provenance, or strict enumeration of external upstream cases.
  The SourceForge CVS ZIP is not the historical mpeg2dec-streams.tar.gz and
  must not be authenticated with that different archive's published MD5.
verify_builds: >
  libmpeg2/0.5.1: SourceForge CVS ZIP SHA-256
  4d42e8eb62bbeb8063ebd0c66a7fb6802b7a9882212c1f7253483f789eb85aa8;
  224 fixtures for 73 test IDs; 5 upstream IGNORE-MD5; recovered manifest
  SHA-256 b22af747d917f8e5fc89ec115116da72c9807330f4f094c5593fa143d79fa3c3;
  same-source x86 73/73 and OHOS W3 integrated Conan create
  libmpeg2-w3-20261006T031522Z upstream 73/73 plus consumer 1/1.
  2026-10-10 integrated OHOS Conan create libmpeg2-w3-20261010T023245Z:
  upstream 73/73 and complete MPEG2-to-RGB24-to-PPM consumer 1/1;
  605-byte official fixture SHA-256
  ab2a5b809a69d9a9e0fbae6b6cb5f9ce461d1fe94065e8fda5ffa81c11bcd22c;
  log SHA-256 379cc3ce8749d03385489b00162453e630dbdf6b314e86dcbb45affa8554c9bf.
authors: codex
source_pr: pending
source_commit: pending
